# Rauf runtime — transient files that must never be tracked
**/.rauf/.loop.lock
**/.rauf/state.json
**/.rauf/DONE
**/.rauf/CANCEL
**/.rauf/iteration-status.json
**/.rauf/rauf.log
**/.rauf/events.ndjson
**/backlog.json.bak

# Claude Code local session config
.claude/
# ...except the agent-kit generator's committed output, which legitimately emits a generated
# `.claude/` tree (the claude ecosystem bundle). It MUST be committed — the generated-drift gate
# compares the committed generated/** set to a fresh regeneration, so an ignored (uncommitted)
# subtree fails CI on a clean checkout. Re-include exactly that path (root `.claude/` stays ignored).
!agent-kit/generated/claude/.claude/
!agent-kit/generated/claude/.claude/**

# Node / TypeScript build artifacts
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment secrets — commit only .env.example, never a real .env (e.g. stack/compose/.env)
.env

# Operator-local compose layer + resolved configs. The override is the operator's own layer
# (host-port exposure, activation mounts — see the bootstrap/rollout-session runbooks); a
# *.resolved.yml is a native config with SecretRefs expanded to PLAINTEXT (alerting activation,
# docs/runbooks/rollout-session.md). Neither is ever tracked.
docker-compose.override.yml
*.resolved.yml

# Local browser screenshots (AGENTS.md: always under ./screenshots); never committed.
screenshots/
# Visual-suite run output (actual/diff images, traces). The committed baselines live in
# apps/web/tests/visual/*-snapshots/ and are generated on CI only.
apps/web/visual-results/

# Private planning and agent-loop state live outside this public repo.
specs/
.rauf/
.rauf.json
forge.config.json
.claude/
.remember/
.handoff/
.system1/
